<%= help_header 'Issue & Task Types' %>

<div class="columns">
  <div class="column">
    <p>
      Issues and Tasks are grouped by <strong>types</strong> (eg. Bug, Feature
      Request, Question).
      <%= link_to 'Admins', user_types_help_path(anchor: 'admins') %> have
      several color and icon options available in order to customize them:
    </p>

    <h3>Color Options</h3>
    <div class="category-tags">
      <% issue_type_color_options.each do |title, name| %>
        <% klass = "issue-type-tag roller-type-color-#{name}" %>
        <%= content_tag :span, class: klass do %>
          <%= content_tag(:span, title) %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <h3>Icon Options</h3>
    <div class="category-tags">
      <% issue_type_icon_options.each do |title, name| %>
        <% klass = "issue-type-tag roller-type-color-default" %>
        <%= content_tag :span, class: klass do %>
          <%= content_tag :i, '', class: "icon-#{name}" %>
          <%= title %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <h3>Priority Levels</h3>
    <p>
      Tasks have a priority level assigned to them that indicate the importance of the bug
      fix, improvement, or new feature. The options are 1 to 4. Here is the quick guide
      of the levels and how they can be used:
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li><strong>Critical</strong> - Most likely tied to a bug that effects many users or clients</li>
      <li><strong>High</strong> - An important bug fix or new improvement</li>
      <li><strong>Medium</strong> - A new feature or improvement</li>
      <li><strong>Low</strong> - A new feature or improvement that can wait</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</div>
